{"id": "K86", "tool": "update_hypothesis", "args": {"hypothesis": "H1", "status": "favored", "confidence": 0.6, "reason": "Survived attempts to break it: no periodicity in V (K61), so no fixed orbiting structure; the neighbour cannot make the optical dips (C14); dips are chromatic in all bands together (C7); the IR excess decays as the optical recovers (C4, C9), and nothing has recurred in 2024-26 (C10). The remaining tension is geometric (C17), not observational. Literature tool failed (K85), so this is formed from data plus my memory of Kenworthy et al. 2023."}, "digest": "6bc0da1f42f96fc3", "author": "claude-opus-5.5", "at": "2026-10-27T06:06:23+00:00"}
{"id": "K87", "tool": "update_hypothesis", "args": {"hypothesis": "H2", "status": "live", "confidence": 0.25, "reason": "Fits the optical part equally well; only less specific about the infrared turn-on. The data cannot distinguish 'collision made the dust' from 'something else made a new dust cloud'."}, "digest": "6bc0da1f42f96fc3", "author": "claude-opus-5.5", "at": "2026-10-27T06:06:25+00:00"}
{"id": "K88", "tool": "update_hypothesis", "args": {"hypothesis": "H3", "status": "disfavored", "confidence": 0.05, "reason": "No periodicity (K61), dips are not grey (C7, C8), and a companion disk does not explain the 1000 K infrared turn-on and decay (C2-C4)."}, "digest": "6bc0da1f42f96fc3", "author": "claude-opus-5.5", "at": "2026-10-27T06:06:26+00:00"}
{"id": "K89", "tool": "update_hypothesis", "args": {"hypothesis": "H4", "status": "disfavored", "confidence": 0.04, "reason": "Rejected for the optical (C14). For the IR it needs a contrived ~5-12x brightening of a field star timed to the target's dimming; cannot be fully excluded without resolved IR data."}, "digest": "6bc0da1f42f96fc3", "author": "claude-opus-5.5", "at": "2026-10-27T06:06:26+00:00"}
{"id": "K90", "tool": "update_hypothesis", "args": {"hypothesis": "H5", "status": "disfavored", "confidence": 0.03, "reason": "The observer's artifacts are real but at the 0.1-0.5 mag level and inconsistent across filters (C11, C12); the 2021-22 event is consistent across filters and physically coloured (C7) and coincides with an independent infrared event (C2, C4). Not rejected only because no second optical source covers the dips within this case (C15)."}, "digest": "6bc0da1f42f96fc3", "author": "claude-opus-5.5", "at": "2026-10-27T06:06:27+00:00"}
{"id": "K91", "tool": "update_hypothesis", "args": {"hypothesis": "H6", "status": "disfavored", "confidence": 0.03, "reason": "No infrared excess before 2018 or after 2023 (C1, C4), and the star is flat to 0.005 mag now (C10), unlike an active dipper."}, "digest": "6bc0da1f42f96fc3", "author": "claude-opus-5.5", "at": "2026-10-27T06:06:28+00:00"}
